HST Office: Word-style Font dialog. Writer's Font tab also holds colour, underline, effects and
superscript/subscript, and the Position page is the "Advanced" tab.

- A dialog opts in with SVX_HST_MERGE_FONT_EFFECTS on the "font" page: SvxCharNamePage then hosts a
  SvxCharEffectsPage and adds no second tab. Other dialogs using these two pages are unchanged.
- Superscript/Subscript exchange SvxEscapementItem with the Advanced page and hide without that item.
- Page id "fonteffects" no longer exists in this dialog; .uno:FontDialog with that page (macros) opens "font".

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
